  <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#018A60" />
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes" />
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent" />
  <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  <style>
    .manual { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px 60px; }
    .manual h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      color: var(--color-primary);
      margin: 28px 0 8px;
      padding-bottom: 4px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    }
    .manual h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 16px; }
    .manual h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-size: var(--text-md);
      color: var(--text-primary);
      margin: 18px 0 6px;
    }
    .manual p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 10px; }
    .manual ul, .manual ol { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; }
    .manual li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .manual code {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
      padding: 1px 5px;
      border-radius: 3px;
      font-size: 0.9em;
      color: var(--color-primary);
    }
    .icon-label {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 4px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
      padding: 2px 8px;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-size: var(--text-xs);
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-primary);
      vertical-align: middle;
    }
    .toc { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 12px; }
    .toc li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .toc a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: none; font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 500; }
    .toc a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="bbq-topnav">
    <a href="/" class="bbq-topnav__logo">
      <img src="/icons/logo.webp" alt="BBQ" width="40" height="40" style="border-radius:6px;" />
    </a>
    <div class="bbq-topnav__title">Manual</div>
    <div class="bbq-topnav__actions"></div>
  </nav>

  <main class="manual">
    <div style="text-align:center; padding:16px 0 8px;">
      <img src="/icons/logo.webp" alt="BBQ" width="64" height="64" style="border-radius:12px;" />
      <h1 style="font-size:var(--text-2xl); color:var(--color-primary); margin:4px 0 0;">BBQ Manual</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted); margin:2px 0 0;">Badminton Batch Queueing</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="toc">
      <li><a href="#what">What BBQ does</a></li>
      <li><a href="#setup">Setting up a game</a></li>
      <li><a href="#registration">Registration and arrival</a></li>
      <li><a href="#courts">Courts tab</a></li>
      <li><a href="#queue">Queue tab</a></li>
      <li><a href="#players">Players tab</a></li>
      <li><a href="#controls">Player controls</a></li>
      <li><a href="#host">Host and co-host actions</a></li>
      <li><a href="#end">Ending a game</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="what">What BBQ does</h2>
    <p>BBQ manages court rotation for casual badminton sessions. It assigns players to courts in fair order, tracks who's playing, who's waiting, and who's on break. No clipboard, no arguments about whose turn it is.</p>
    <p>One person acts as the host. Everyone else opens the app on their phone to check their spot in the queue.</p>

    <h2 id="setup">Setting up a game</h2>
    <p>Only the host sets up a game. Go to the home screen. Fill in the date, number of courts, and a game name if you want one. Set a 4-digit PIN to protect host actions. Tap <strong>Create Game</strong>.</p>
    <p>The PIN keeps players from messing with court assignments. Share it with trusted people to make them co-hosts — anyone with the PIN has full host access.</p>
    <p>Each court holds up to 8 players: 4 playing, 4 in the next rotation.</p>

    <h2 id="registration">Registration and arrival</h2>

    <h3>Before game day</h3>
    <p>Share the <span class="icon-label"><i class="bi bi-qr-code"></i> QR</span> code from the Games list. Players scan it and register their name and skill level (Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced). Players must register before game day — no walk-ins.</p>
    <p>Registration locks in a spot but doesn't put anyone in the queue yet. That happens on arrival.</p>

    <h3>At the venue</h3>
    <p>Display the Arrival QR at the courts. Registered players scan it to check in. Once checked in, they enter the queue and start waiting for a court.</p>

    <h2 id="courts">Courts tab</h2>
    <p>Shows each court's current state.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ready</strong> — players are assigned, waiting for the match to start.</li>
      <li><span class="icon-label"><i class="bi bi-play-fill"></i> Blinking</span> — match in progress. A timer tracks how long it's been running. After 15 minutes the timer turns amber. After 20 it turns red.</li>
      <li><strong>Waiting for players</strong> — not enough players in the queue to fill the court.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Starting and ending matches</h3>
    <p>Any player assigned to a court, or the host/co-host, can tap <strong>START MATCH</strong>. Once someone taps it, the button locks — no one else can tap it again. This prevents double-taps.</p>
    <p>When the match is done, the button changes to <strong>END MATCH</strong>. Same rule: one person taps it, it locks. Whoever ends the match enters the score. After that, the next batch of players rotates in automatically.</p>

    <h2 id="queue">Queue tab</h2>
    <p>The queue shows upcoming court assignments. Each batch card displays:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which court the batch is assigned to.</li>
      <li>Team A and Team B splits.</li>
      <li>How long the longest-waiting player has been queued.</li>
      <li>Status: <strong>Get Ready</strong> (next up), <strong>Up Next</strong>, <strong>In Queue</strong>, or <strong>Looking for Players</strong> if the batch is short.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>BBQ assigns players first-come, first-served. The algorithm handles team composition and court allocation automatically.</p>
    <p><a href="/queue-explained" style="color:var(--color-primary);">How the queueing system works →</a></p>

    <h2 id="players">Players tab</h2>
    <p>Lists every player who has checked in. Each card shows their name, skill level, arrival time, and current court (if playing).</p>
    <p>Filter pills at the top let you narrow the list: Registered, Arrived, Playing, Waiting, Break, Skipped, Left.</p>

    <h2 id="controls">Player controls</h2>
    <p>Each player card has three buttons: <span class="icon-label" style="background:var(--color-primary); color:#fff;"><i class="bi bi-play-fill"></i></span> Play, <span class="icon-label" style="background:#D97706; color:#fff;"><i class="bi bi-pause-fill"></i></span> Pause, and <span class="icon-label" style="background:var(--color-danger); color:#fff;"><i class="bi bi-stop-fill"></i></span> Stop. The lit button shows the player's current state.</p>

    <h3>What each button means</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Play (green)</strong> — player is in the queue or on a court.</li>
      <li><strong>Pause (amber)</strong> — on break. Out of the queue until they tap Play again. Players can do this themselves.</li>
      <li><strong>Stop (red)</strong> — left for the night. Out of the queue permanently. Only the host can stop another player.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Host-only buttons</h3>
    <p>Two extra buttons appear for the host in specific situations:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="icon-label"><i class="bi bi-fast-forward-fill"></i></span> <strong>Skip</strong> — appears next to waiting players. Moves them to the back of the queue. Useful when someone stepped away without pausing.</li>
      <li><span class="icon-label"><i class="bi bi-rewind-fill"></i></span> <strong>Rewind</strong> — appears next to skipped players. Puts them back in the queue at their original position.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These buttons are hidden for regular players and only show when relevant.</p>

    <h2 id="host">Host and co-host actions</h2>
    <p>Enter the 4-digit PIN to unlock host controls. Anyone with the PIN is a co-host and gets the same access. The host/co-host can:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Skip or rewind players.</li>
      <li>Stop another player (mark them as left).</li>
      <li>Add or remove courts (using the +/− buttons at the top of Courts tab).</li>
      <li>End the entire session.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Starting and ending matches on a court doesn't require the PIN. Any player assigned to the court can do it too. The host/co-host can also start or end matches on any court.</p>
    <p>Without the PIN, players can pause/unpause themselves and view the queue, but can't skip others or change settings.</p>

    <h2 id="end">Ending a game</h2>
    <p>Scroll to the bottom of the Courts tab. Tap <strong>End Game</strong>. Confirm. A summary screen shows the session stats: total matches played, hours, number of players, top 3 winners, and first 3 arrivals.</p>
    <p>This can't be undone. The session disappears from the Games list on the home screen.</p>

    <div style="text-align:center; padding:24px 0 0; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:var(--text-xs);">
      BBQ v1.0 — made for Friday night badminton.
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
